sentences.l:
And there came on a beggar, a public one, who through the town
of Ithaca used to beg, and stood out among them for a frenzied belly
unceasingly to eat and to drink;

But with hands do not at all too much challenge me, do not anger me,
lest, old man though I am, you, chest and lips, I smear
with blood;

“Stranger, if heart and manly spirit urge you
to ward this man off, of the others not any of the Achaeans
fear, since with more he will fight who strikes you;

“Now may you neither be, braggart, nor ever have been born,
if this man indeed you tremble at and fear terribly,
an old man, afflicted with distress, which comes upon him.

Then, both having raised their hands, the one struck the right shoulder,
Irus, and the other the neck beneath the ear, and the bones within
he crushed;

and at once came through his mouth red blood,
and he fell down in the dust, crying out, and gnashed his teeth together,
kicking the ground with his feet;

But Odysseus
dragged him through the forecourt, having taken him by the foot, until he reached the courtyard,
and the doors of the portico;
